    "answer": "The axial skeleton consists of **80 bones**. Its main components are: (1) Skull, cranium (8 bones) + facial bones (14 bones); (2) Vertebral column, 26 vertebrae; (3) Thoracic cage, 12 pairs of ribs + sternum.",
